<figure class="art-fig art-fig--seq">
<svg viewBox="0 0 480 330" role="img" aria-label="How the 50 Percent Rule reaches companies that are not on the SDN list" aria-describedby="f50-d" font-family="inherit"><desc id="f50-d">Blocked person X, on the SDN list, owns 50 percent of company A. Company A owns 50 percent of company B. Under OFAC's 50 Percent Rule both A and B are blocked, although neither is named on the SDN list. This is the example in OFAC FAQ 401.</desc><defs><marker id="f50-a" viewBox="0 0 10 10" refX="8" refY="5" markerWidth="7" markerHeight="7" orient="auto"><path d="M0 0 L10 5 L0 10z" fill="var(--muted)"/></marker></defs>
<rect x="1" y="34" width="124" height="70" rx="12" fill="var(--accent-soft)" stroke="var(--accent)" stroke-width="2"/><text x="63.0" y="64" text-anchor="middle" font-size="18" font-weight="700" fill="var(--ink)">Person X</text><text x="63.0" y="88" text-anchor="middle" font-size="15" fill="var(--muted)">on SDN list</text>
<path d="M129 69 L173 69" stroke="var(--muted)" stroke-width="2" marker-end="url(#f50-a)"/><text x="152.0" y="24" text-anchor="middle" font-size="15" font-weight="700" fill="var(--muted)">50%</text>
<rect x="179" y="34" width="124" height="70" rx="12" fill="var(--accent-soft)" stroke="var(--accent)" stroke-width="2" stroke-dasharray="6 5"/><text x="241.0" y="64" text-anchor="middle" font-size="18" font-weight="700" fill="var(--ink)">Company A</text><text x="241.0" y="88" text-anchor="middle" font-size="15" fill="var(--muted)">not listed</text>
<path d="M307 69 L351 69" stroke="var(--muted)" stroke-width="2" marker-end="url(#f50-a)"/><text x="330.0" y="24" text-anchor="middle" font-size="15" font-weight="700" fill="var(--muted)">50%</text>
<rect x="357" y="34" width="124" height="70" rx="12" fill="var(--accent-soft)" stroke="var(--accent)" stroke-width="2" stroke-dasharray="6 5"/><text x="419.0" y="64" text-anchor="middle" font-size="18" font-weight="700" fill="var(--ink)">Company B</text><text x="419.0" y="88" text-anchor="middle" font-size="15" fill="var(--muted)">not listed</text>
<text x="0" y="146" font-size="18" font-weight="700" fill="var(--accent)">All three are blocked</text>
<text x="0" y="180" font-size="17" fill="var(--body)">A is 50% owned by a blocked person,</text>
<text x="0" y="207" font-size="17" fill="var(--body)">so A is blocked. B is 50% owned by A,</text>
<text x="0" y="234" font-size="17" fill="var(--body)">so B is blocked too. Neither company is</text>
<text x="0" y="261" font-size="17" fill="var(--body)">on the list: only ownership data finds them.</text>
<rect x="1" y="300" width="20" height="16" rx="3" fill="var(--accent-soft)" stroke="var(--accent)" stroke-width="2"/><text x="30" y="313" font-size="15" fill="var(--muted)">listed</text><rect x="100" y="300" width="20" height="16" rx="3" fill="var(--accent-soft)" stroke="var(--accent)" stroke-width="2" stroke-dasharray="4 3"/><text x="129" y="313" font-size="15" fill="var(--muted)">blocked, not on the list</text>
</svg>
<figcaption>The ownership example from OFAC FAQ 401. Stakes held by several blocked persons are added together.</figcaption></figure>
